release. Measured across 22 Jiras, it cut ticket-resolution time by 45% and root-cause-analysis time by 55%, and it was selected for trade-secret protection.","vector":{"10":0.119,"20":0.1367,"22":0.1367,"45":0.1367,"55":0.1367,"maestro":0.2015,"multi":0.1504,"agent":0.1803,"ticket":0.2868,"resolution":0.2314,"portable":0.1367,"platform":0.119,"ayush":0.0587,"built":0.0888,"cadence":0.0968,"conductor":0.1367,"orchestrates":0.1367,"specialist":0.1367,"ai":0.0821,"agents":0.1065,"across":0.1803,"phase":0.1367,"human":0.1367,"gated":0.1367,"workflow":0.1367,"carries":0.1367,"xcelium":0.0888,"engineering":0.0821,"intake":0.1367,"root":0.2314,"cause":0.2314,"analysis":0.1803,"through":0.1065,"fix":0.1367,"validation":0.1367,"review":0.119,"regression":0.0968,"release":0.119,"measured":0.1367,"jiras":0.1367,"cut":0.119,"time":0.2015,"selected":0.1367,"trade":0.1367,"secret":0.1367,"protection":0.1367}},{"id":"xcelium-agents","source":"Projects · ChipStack Xcelium AI Agents","title":"ChipStack Xcelium AI agents for performance and memory","text":"For Cadence ChipStack AI, Ayush built multi-agent Python workflows on the OpenAI Agents SDK that profile Xcelium simulations and apply and verify performance and memory fixes, achieving a 31.3% simulation speedup on a validated benchmark. A deterministic-first re-architecture cut end-to-end runtime from 148.3 s to 76.8 s (1.93x) and analysis from 71.1 s to 18.0 s (3.9x). He also built the shared agent framework with typed state, checkpoint and resume, structured outputs and fallback recovery, plus a YAML-driven LLM-as-judge regression framework.","vector":{"18":0.1297,"31":0.1297,"71":0.1297,"76":0.1297,"148":0.1297,"chipstack":0.1912,"xcelium":0.1428,"ai":0.132,"agents":0.1711,"performance":0.1227,"memory":0.2196,"cadence":0.0919,"ayush":0.0557,"built":0.1428,"multi":0.0843,"agent":0.1711,"python":0.113,"workflows":0.1297,"openai":0.1297,"sdk":0.1297,"profile":0.113,"simulations":0.1297,"apply":0.1297,"verify":0.1297,"fixes":0.12